1
00:00:00,088 --> 00:00:03,718
(Sheldon:)My new computer came with
Windows 7.

2
00:00:04,718 --> 00:00:08,928
(Sheldon:)Windows 7 is much more user-friendly
than Windows Vista.

3
00:00:09,097 --> 00:00:11,097
(Sheldon:)I don't like that.

4
00:00:14,603 --> 00:00:18,773
(Leonard:)Don't you think looking for a new city
to live in is a bit of an overreaction?

5
00:00:18,940 --> 00:00:20,980
(Sheldon:)Our apartment was broken into.

6
00:00:21,151 --> 00:00:23,231
(Sheldon:)Our security system tried to kill me.

7
00:00:23,403 --> 00:00:28,113
(Sheldon:)And as a result, I'm leaving Pasadena
forever. Tell me how that's overreacting.

8
00:00:28,742 --> 00:00:32,162
(Penny:)Come on, Sheldon. You can't move.
Don't you need to stay in one place...

9
00:00:32,329 --> 00:00:35,789
(Penny:)...so the mother ship can find you
when it returns?

10
00:00:36,333 --> 00:00:39,003
(Sheldon:)Oh, if that were only true.

11
00:00:39,169 --> 00:00:42,259
(Sheldon:)Unfortunately, as I'm earthbound
for the foreseeable future...

12
00:00:42,422 --> 00:00:45,092
(Sheldon:)...I need to find a location
that's more hospitable...

13
00:00:45,258 --> 00:00:49,758
(Sheldon:)...than the mean streets of Pasadena.
Like Enid, Oklahoma.

14
00:00:50,597 --> 00:00:54,477
(Sheldon:)Low crime rate,
and high-speed Internet connectivity...

15
00:00:54,643 --> 00:00:57,813
...but no model-train shops.

16
00:00:58,980 --> 00:01:04,020
(Sheldon:)Sorry, Enid.

